        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waitsburg%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1881 the Oregon Railroad and Navigation Company completed a line through Waitsburg, linking it to Walla Walla.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waitsburg%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s historic district, dating to the 1880s, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waitsburg%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Waitsburg Historical Society began restoring the Bruce House in 1971, a project that still continues today.",
